= render 'admin/breadcrumb_header'

- documents = @response.documents

.admin-registry.my-3
  %header.admin-registry__head
    %span.admin-registry__title
      %i.fa-solid.fa-trash-can-arrow-up{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
      Tombstoned items
      - if documents.any?
        %span.admin-registry__count= pluralize(documents.size, 'item')
    .admin-registry__head-actions
      %span.admin-registry__subtitle
        - if current_user&.admin?
          %i.fa-solid.fa-lock{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
          Admin-only
        - else
          %i.fa-solid.fa-user-shield{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
          Delegated admin access

  .p-3
    %p.text-muted.small.mb-0
      Every tombstoned Work, Collection and Community. Restoring reverses the tombstone — the item becomes discoverable again and its History records the restore. A Collection or Community can only be restored once any tombstoned parent above it is restored.
    - if current_user&.admin?
      %p.text-muted.small.mb-0.mt-2
        Permanent deletion is the other way out of a withdrawal, and nothing reverses it: it removes the item and every preserved copy of its files, earlier versions included, leaving only the audit record. A Collection or Community must be emptied first, and its tombstoned members count.

  - if documents.any?
    .table-responsive
      %table.table.table-borderless.admin-registry-table
        %thead
          %tr
            %th{scope: 'col'} Title
            %th{scope: 'col'} Type
            %th{scope: 'col'} PID
            %th{scope: 'col'}
        %tbody
          - documents.each do |doc|
            %tr
              %td
                .admin-registry-table__name= finder_doc_heading(doc)
              %td= finder_type_chip(doc.klass_type)
              %td
                %span.admin-registry-table__id= doc.to_param
              %td.text-end
                .d-inline-flex.gap-3.align-items-center
                  = button_to restore_admin_tombstone_path(doc.to_param), params: { type: doc.klass_type }, class: 'admin-registry-table__edit admin-registry-table__edit--restore', form: { class: 'd-inline', data: { turbo_confirm: "Restore “#{finder_doc_title(doc)}”? It will be discoverable again.", turbo_confirm_title: 'Confirm restore', turbo_confirm_button: 'Restore', turbo_confirm_variant: 'primary' } } do
                    %i.fa-solid.fa-rotate-left{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
                    Restore
                  - if current_user&.admin?
                    = button_to admin_tombstone_path(doc.to_param), method: :delete, params: { type: doc.klass_type }, class: 'admin-registry-table__edit admin-registry-table__edit--purge', form: { class: 'd-inline', data: { turbo_confirm: tombstone_purge_confirm(doc), turbo_confirm_title: 'Confirm permanent deletion', turbo_confirm_button: 'Delete permanently' } } do
                      %i.fa-solid.fa-trash-can{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
                      Delete permanently

    - if @response.respond_to?(:total_pages) && @response.total_pages > 1
      .px-3.pt-2
        = paginate @response
  - else
    .admin-registry__empty
      %i.fa-solid.fa-trash-can-arrow-up.admin-registry__empty-icon{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
      %p.mb-1.fw-semibold.text-body Nothing is tombstoned
      %p.mb-0.small.text-muted
        When a Work, Collection or Community is tombstoned, it appears here so it can be restored.
